      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "ENA 3734.12 recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>[God], whose holy Temple and place will be rebuilt amidst the righteous; who grants</li>\n<li>his adherents victory over his enemies and sustains the reign of their kings; who</li>\n<li>hearkens to those whose intentions are sincere, and accepts the prayers of those who are close to him;</li>\n<li>who accepts the sacrifices and prayers of the righteous and their kings</li>\n<li>by granting his blessing to them in this world and the next; who accepts the gratitude of</li>\n<li>those who thank him with sincerity for the benefits that he has rendered to them; who</li>\n<li>always grants well-being to his adherents, his sincere friends, and his pious devotees.</li>\n<li>When the most illustrious vizier (al-waz\u012br al-ajall)</li>\n<li>Ya\u02bfq\u016bb ibn Y\u016bsuf, may God sustain his high station, showed me a translation</li>\n<li>made by a certain Jewish translator of the \"Book of Prayers and</li>\n<li>Blessings\" following the prescribed laws,</li>\n<li>which [that translator] translated from the language of the Hebrews into the language of the Arabs,</li>\n<li>employing both Arabic language and script, neither he nor the company of</li>\n<li>thinkers&mdash;consisting of litterateurs who deal with Kal\u0101m and</li>\n<li>philosophy as well as physicians present at the session in which religions are discussed (<i>majlis al-kal\u0101m \u02bfal\u0101 al-shar\u0101\u02bei\u02bf</i>), [all of whom] meet regularly at his court&mdash;</li>\n<li>ought to have vilified, ridiculed,</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
